  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nFor nearly the entire week, the prevailing large-scale pattern will \nfeature mid-level troughing across the Pacific Coast with ridging \ncentered from the Central Plains to the Middle Mississippi Valley. A \ngradual warmup is forecast through the week as LREF 850mb \ntemperatures slowly climb from near 10C at the beginning of the week \ninto the low teens (10-14C) by mid-late week. The NBM continues to \nbe on the warmer end of guidance but has come down a few degrees on \nthe latest run. Now it is more closely aligned with other members \nand more representable of the low-level airmass (850mb temperatures) \nthat the LREF indicates. As a result, the latest LREF temperature \nIQRs reveal near normal temperatures are expected into Tuesday with \nabove normal temperatures forecast to make a comeback by Thursday \nlasting into next Saturday. Mid-level ridging remains nearly \nstationary across the area this week, resulting in high confidence \nthat dry conditions prevail into next Saturday.",
